  "id": "COMPOUND:307 - PROTEIN:1653",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which gefitinib may interact with Tyrosine-protein kinase Fgr, through a series of molecular interactions involving flavopiridol and staurosporine. Gefitinib is reported to target Transmembrane glycoprotein NMB and IL13 protein, both of which are subsequently targeted by flavopiridol, which in turn inhibits Tyrosine-protein kinase Fgr. Similarly, gefitinib is also reported to target PT-45, which is inhibited by staurosporine, leading to the inhibition of Tyrosine-protein kinase Fgr. These findings indicate that gefitinib may act through a pathway where its targets are first modulated by flavopiridol or staurosporine, thereby influencing the activity of Tyrosine-protein kinase Fgr. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between gefitinib and Fgr, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The presence of multiple independent pathways suggests that the inhibition of Fgr may be a downstream effect of these interactions, potentially through shared regulatory mechanisms or different modes of action.",
